Ah, I understand perfectly! By default, Material UI hides the 3 vertical dots (the column menu icon) to keep the headers looking "clean," and they only appear when you hover your mouse over them.
If you want those 3 dots to be **permanently visible** so users instantly know they can click them to filter, we just need to override the default CSS behavior in your DataGrid styles.
Here is exactly what you need to add to your styles object at the very top of both **VoucherPostingStatus.js** and **VoucherAuthorization.js** (if you want it on both screens).
### The Fix
Find your dataGridContainer inside the styles object at the top of the file, and add the two lines targeting the .MuiDataGrid-menuIcon to force it to always be visible.
**Replace your current dataGridContainer with this:**
```javascript
  dataGridContainer: {
    height: 600,
    width: "100%",
    backgroundColor: "background.paper",
    boxShadow: 2,
    borderRadius: 2,
    border: 1,
    borderColor: "divider",
    "& .MuiDataGrid-columnHeaders": {
      backgroundColor: (theme) => alpha(theme.palette.primary.main, 0.08),
      fontWeight: "bold",
      fontSize: "0.95rem",
    },
    "& .MuiDataGrid-row:hover": {
      backgroundColor: (theme) => alpha(theme.palette.primary.main, 0.04),
    },
    // --- ADD THESE TWO BLOCKS TO KEEP THE 3 DOTS ALWAYS VISIBLE ---
    "& .MuiDataGrid-menuIcon": {
      visibility: "visible !important",
      width: "auto !important",
    },
    "& .MuiDataGrid-iconButtonContainer": {
      visibility: "visible !important",
      width: "auto !important",
    },
  },

```
### Why this works:
MUI actively applies visibility: hidden and width: 0 to that icon container until a hover event occurs. By explicitly passing visibility: "visible" !important inside the DataGrid's sx prop, we completely disable the hover-to-show behavior, forcing the 3 vertical dots to stay permanently pinned next to the column titles!
